  "policies": [
    "Shadow Ascendant declares an owner end-turn subject. Its fresh body selects one other currently active/live friendly ordinary minion, one physical weight each, then applies one ordinary +1/+1 Buff. Empty candidates use no RNG; natural end-turn/repeat admission remains the existing engine policy.",
    "Tower listens to its own positive actual damage_dealt. A captured takes-damage notification does not add a survives-damage condition. Two attributed fixed Frail Ghoul requests use existing quantity/capacity/death rules; those are the unchanged native Charge/end-turn-death children, not vanilla tokens.",
    "Specter has native Taunt and existing cannot_attack policy, with both Undead and Draenei printed tribes. Silence and forced attacks retain existing policy/lifecycle rules; no invented keyword.",
    "Liferender targets an enemy board minion iff the executing player has a genuine remaining-health transition on the current global turn. The pure target profile and actual body query the same original hero-health ledger, not damage alone, cumulative own-turn count, current missing health or host event log. No change gives targetless play; active condition uses IF_AVAILABLE. Pre-payment target eligibility and actual body execution are distinct existing windows; no late target is invented.",
    "Lingering Spirit uses native Reborn and original deathrattle controller. Heal own hero3 with EFFECT healing; only actual original HealthResult.overheal produces a fresh random-enemy MINION_ABILITY damage packet. Converted/prevented/redirected results never reconstruct excess from requested amount or missing health. Existing numeric health modifiers, reactions, checkpoints and lifecycle remain authoritative.",
    "Exact end/damage/death/conditional-target/overheal timing and special hero policies remain local M6 pending CN calibration. Current official faces and class-set availability do not close formal M0 or generator legality. No incomplete random generation pool is opened."
  ]
